{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/314143-the-hardest-games-to-run-and-why","id":314143,"title":"The Hardest Games to Run and Why","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-11-16T19:37:27-08:00","id":314143,"title":"The Hardest Games to Run and Why","content":"So, i been reading some books here and there, the only ones i havent tackled yet are Mummy, Changeling and Orpheus (not concidering the Dark Ages) and i been wondering...since theres so many books and so much information, which one you concider the hardest to run and why?<br /> <br /> Mage The Ascension: probably because how open the game is and how Metaphisical can get, not concidering the high ammount of books<br /> Wraith: probably because how Rough the game is for some players so its not a matter of a high ammount of books, but rather how hard is to get players willing to go down with The Grey Book of Depression<br /> Vampire the Masquerade: because HOLY SHIT THE AMMOUNT OF BOOKS YOU NEED TO READ!, i mean...i like to follow the cannon and i want to make it feel as authentic as possible..but sweet mother theresa on the hood of a mercedes benz theres a lot of info to cover..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-16T20:51:59-08:00","id":314174,"title":"","content":"Hrm.<br /> <br /> VtM and WtA are really only as hard as you make it on yourself. Sure they have huge libraries of stuff. Lots of messy metaplot, and all that. But really you can skip so much of that and just run the basics. Their themes are fairly strait forward and most of the time the rules don't get in the way.<br /> <br /> Mage seems hard, and I'm a bit biased because I've run it a lot, but it is more intimidating than difficult. There's some things the books don't explain, but there's plenty of discussion of online (ex: HOP vs. HAP, RBD vs PBD). There's a lot of pressure on the ST to be consistent and fair on these things, but getting caught up on the metaphysics is something of a trap. It's easy to do, but you really just want to avoid it. They're backdrop more than focus when it comes to actual play. Mage's rules do have some serious gaps in supporting &quot;end game&quot; issues like altering paradigms and such, but if you're sticking to the basic level of the game those aren't such a bit deal.<br /> <br /> WtO is definitely hard on thematic points due to the dark nature of what it deals with. It also has Shadow play, which can be really hard. With the right group, WtO is great. But it's easy to cross a line and make it not fun.<br /> <br /> CtD's should be easier to play but the muddled themes and very poor mechanics make it very annoying to do so. Lots of very key concepts and rules just are not well implemented in the game. I know this game has a lot of very adamant fans... but as written it is actually very rough to run. It's definitely towards my top end of the ones there.<br /> <br /> KotE mostly depends on if your group is turned off by the very poor themes it presents. The mechanics have issues, balance is poor even by cWOD standards, there's too many things to track, but it works in play if you pay attention to it. If the themes get in the way? Nightmare to run. If not, passable.<br /> <br /> HtR runs pretty smoothly as long as you remember to not let the canon stuff from the other games bleed too much into it. It can get kinda messy at the higher level (if the characters survive that long!) with lots of Derangements from high Virtues. It's straightforward and has enough options to be interesting with a few different approaches.<br /> <br /> MtR suffers mostly from a lack of material and relying a bit much on knowing the cWOD pretty well. Like KotE the rules work, if a bit wonky in places. It's nice for a change of pace if you play a lot of the cWOD games but don't want to leave the cWOD completely.<br /> <br /> DtF isn't so bad. It's harder than VtM and WtA, mostly because a lack of material and no chance to clean up some of its only edition screw ups in the rules. It's a bit ridiculous in a few places, but in a pure Demons game they at least aren't a big deal.<br /> <br /> Orpheus is pretty simple. It's got a built in adventure and works without it. The rules are pretty solid. It's like HtR in many ways, but a bit better integrated into the larger cWOD. Some of the powers can be a bit odd to wrap your head around at first. But since you don't get too many of them, you get an chance to work them out.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-16T22:48:14-08:00","id":314273,"title":"","content":"I think the most difficult is WtO. In all other settings your players still spend most of game time in &quot;reality&quot; that resembles our real world, therefore they're not lost what to do and the storyteller is also able to improvise pretty easily. In WtO on the other side... (pun intended) you start in a completely different world thats some kinda mirror-land to reality at best. The Storyteller has to get into a whole new world that tries not to interact with the quick and even punishes it. IIRC every other splat may hide from humans for different reasons but none of them is punished simply for interacting with them and almost all of them use humans as servants, allies or at least as food.<br /> <br /> I'd really love to play WtO anyway, but never found the right people for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1235-eadee","name":"Eadee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-16T23:06:38-08:00","id":314277,"title":"","content":"Wraith is the hardest by far. People can't wrap their heads around it and it's too damn depressing for most; hell, my depression is most of the reason I like the damn game. It's impossible to pitch to people and the emotional investment is too damn much. People want to play for fun and Wraith just isn't that.<br /> <br /> Still one of my favorite games of all time, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T04:41:25-08:00","id":314374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Vampire the Masquerade: because HOLY SHIT THE AMMOUNT OF BOOKS YOU NEED TO READ!, i mean...i like to follow the cannon and i want to make it feel as authentic as possible..but sweet mother theresa on the hood of a mercedes benz theres a lot of info to cover.. </div> </div> </div>Seriously, if in your case you cannot be bothered to read all those books because of more important stuff to do (because all we do have stuff to do and lack of time is understandable), I recommend focusing on corebook info foremostly, and then ask yourself what kind of info you specifically need for a chronicle and limit your choices. It took me months after all to catch up on with anything I wanted to know in OWoD. We can always help you narrow down here. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T05:36:36-08:00","id":314406,"title":"","content":"The hardest game to run is the one your players known nothing about. <br /> If my players are new to a game or don't own many or any of the books from that line then I tend to stick by CoreBook and pick from other books as I go.<br /> If they own (or have borrowed and read up on) the game and source books etc then the game becomes easier and I typically allow for more immediate inclusion of other materials. They've probably already got concepts and ideas brewing, they understand the mythos of the game line and need less explanation on things their characters should know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T11:50:00-08:00","id":314733,"title":"","content":"Demon the Fallen is probably the hardest game I've ever seen since the rules are just so damn terrible. <br /> Mummy is a close second in terms of painful, not because of the damn rules being awful but because the game is full of lingo that's so hard to keep in your head. You basically have to read the CRB, then the Companion, then the CRB while keeping your finger on the Lexicon page. It's super easy to understand once you know what all the lingo means, but it's like reading another language.<br /> Mage isn't terrible, just complicated and comes down to a lot of ST ruling. There's just a lot of possibilities for what you can do, and you need to remember your players are GOD DAMN WIZARDS, so rules shouldn't be standing in their way too much.<br /> Changling, just not going to touch that with a 30ft pole. <br /> KotE is probably tied or slightly worse than Mummy since it's bad rules + a hybrid of Revised and 2e + terrible wording + weird lingo.<br /> Vampire is a pretty straight forward system, balance is just the hardest thing to deal with. <br /> Hunter is pretty simple but it's played best by newbies who've never been in an OWoD game before. <br /> Werewolf is actually probably the easiest system, combat rules are the best flat out, character development is everywhere, and the rules are pretty solid. <br /> Wraith I've never played before but the rules seem like you need a good group before even playing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1VN49Y7tH2ZV0l7Hx65RWX1ez-Q9Lst-8ZTyTJeCTpxM/\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerer 20th</a> homebrew and my update to <a href=\"http://immortalthegathering.blogspot.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Highlander: the Gathering</a> for 20th Anniversary edition.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2414-theoutlander523","name":"theoutlander523","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T12:29:32-08:00","id":315622,"title":"","content":"Changeling definitely hardest to run for me, mainly because it's quite difficult to come up with solid story hooks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2214-traveller","name":"Traveller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2214_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-19T15:11:43-08:00","id":316556,"title":"","content":"Said it before, I'll say it again..........f'ing Changeling and that Chimerical reality versus Reality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-20T05:55:22-08:00","id":317324,"title":"","content":"For me it's Changeling (as a ST).<br /> <br /> Wraith is good IF you have an already established group to play with, and there is a level of trust among them personally. Otherwise, it is basically impossible.<br /> <br /> Mage is the hardest to explain to new players. Oddly enough, I find that people entirely new to RPing get it faster than old RPers new to Mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/PbrO9Kq.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2211-sixfootchicken","name":"SixFootChicken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2211_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"559"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-20T07:09:09-08:00","id":317350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SixFootChicken</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/314143-the-hardest-games-to-run-and-why?p=317324#post317324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oddly enough, I find that people entirely new to RPing get it faster than old RPers new to Mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wonder if it has anything to do with most newbies thinking their characters can do just about anything (and in Mage, they CAN), while the experienced players have learned they have limitations and rules and they have trouble getting past that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-20T07:21:54-08:00","id":317354,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\">The hardest games, I found, to get off the ground are (in descending order, most difficult first):<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">Werewolf:</span></b> I could never sell my troupe on WtA. I think the Umbra was the biggest obstacle to overcome. Every time I brought up the spirit world, someone would start doing a recital of the Peyote-Vision-Quest scene from <i>Young Guns</i>.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">Mage: </span></b> I\u2019ve *made* several Mage characters (Union and Traditions) and even started to play them. Unfortunately (and this is just my experience) the sessions quickly devolved into debates about philosophy and physics. <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">Changeling: </span></b> I love CtD and wish I could have played more than a few one-shots (or a bizarre set of crossovers that kinda resembled CtD). I could never get the buy-in from my troupe to give it a try. When brought up, someone would inevitably start singing (from Sesame Street) <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">\u201cOne of these things is not like the other.\u201d</span><br /> <br /> Oddly, WtO was an easy sell for my troupe. </span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-20T07:42:42-08:00","id":317368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/314143-the-hardest-games-to-run-and-why?p=317350#post317350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wonder if it has anything to do with most newbies thinking their characters can do just about anything (and in Mage, they CAN), while the experienced players have learned they have limitations and rules and they have trouble getting past that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah I think that is basically it. Experienced RPers want finite lists and descriptions of what they can and can not do, what the system is, and how it's used. Then they take those rigid powers and try to apply them in creative ways - which is basically the premise (mechanically) of every single game EXCEPT Mage: the Ascension.<br /> <br /> New RPers think: &quot;OHH okay so I am a chemist who can push science so far that I can mess with Matter in weird ways. Can I use some acid to turn lead into gold?&quot; and really take off with the dynamic magic aspect of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/PbrO9Kq.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2211-sixfootchicken","name":"SixFootChicken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2211_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"559"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-20T09:11:41-08:00","id":317430,"title":"","content":"Seems I'm a bit divergent from most folks here, but that's mostly because I'm one of those Changeling fans. Half of my troupe is made of of folks who both ST and play, and all of us can throw out a Changeling game off the cuff.<br /> <br /> For me, I think the hardest is probly Mage. Mostly because I can't seem to nail down a story line that's interesting or cohesive. Either I need to include 2-3 of the other settings, or halfway through the story Paradox backlash breaks my players' reality down and no one can remember what they were doing in the first place. It's always messy to tie together. It's always easy for me to teach people Mage, it's always hard for me to get people to focus on anything while they're busy messing around with the fabric of reality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4297-explodingjoe","name":"ExplodingJoe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4297_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-22T23:54:55-08:00","id":319683,"title":"","content":"For me, as an online gamer, Changeling the Dreaming. And not for all the reasons stated here.<br /> <br /> The major problem with CtD as a game is that it tries to wear far too many hats before even establishing what it really wants to be in the first place. First you have the 'dream is dying' hat, which paints the dreaming as basically a soon to be dying thing and the remaining changelings as refugees who stick together and try to eke out what little living they can. Banality bites like a motherfucker if you try to do anything special and Undoing is always around the corner. Each kith is closer to a high school clique than an actual magical race and things are very light on fantasy.<br /> <br /> Then you have the 'War on Concordia' aspect, which basically takes everything of the previous aspect and puts it in the bin. Suddenly, the fox holes and ratty freeholds become these castles with sieges and histories. Suddenly you have a massive cultural scars between the Sidhe and the Commers. In this aspect, the game is clearly a fantasy game with WoD aspects and darkness.This is the version I think most people use.<br /> <br /> And then there's the larger metaplot of Winter Coming (insert Sean Bean here). I have not explored this much, myself, sadly.<br /> <br /> All of this would be fine, but each aspect cancels out the other. Unlike in Mage, which juggles all its different aspects like a master, Changeling started with a certain theme which it then could not make into a larger game. And each writer seems to have their own takes on the setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-01T20:10:51-08:00","id":327618,"title":"","content":"I am going to go with Vampire, actually. Honestly the sort of political intrigue that Vampire is supposed to be about is very hard to do properly and requires a lot of work by the ST to make it feel real and dynamic. Plus it's a challenge to keep players from being desensitized to their characters' desensitization. &quot;Yeah, yeah, I eat the hobo and heal. Do I still need a Humanity check? Plllb.&quot;<br /> <br /> Werewolf is D&amp;D. Can you run D&amp;D? Then you can run Werewolf. There's monsters, there's magic items, there's levels, there's spells, it's D&amp;D. You can get mad about that and talk about themes and real role-playing and such, but it's a solid way to run things.<br /> <br /> Mage is really so open to possibility, the only things you need are knowing when to say no and players with some kind of unified direction. You have power! Go use it! Fly to Mars! Save the whales! Murderize some Reality Deviants! Stick it to the man!<br /> <br /> Wraith is equally versatile. You can do really human stories with Wraith. Or you can do great revenge plots. Or you can go on a heroic, epic Odyssey, possibly with Odysseus. Or it can be D&amp;D, with literally the best dungeon ever made.<br /> <br /> Changeling is just questing. Save this guy, find this Macguffin, slay this beast, once again the day is safe for the Dreaming. Easy peasy. Also dicking with mundanes because it's fun and you can get away with it.<br /> <br /> Hunter: There is a mystery. The party finds out it's a monster (or sometimes not, to shake things up). Party gets it's ass kicked. Party then researches to find more about the monster. Party returns to kill/seal away/banish/redeem the monster. Rinse and repeat.<br /> <br /> Demon is Vampire, but with more stuff and more things to do. So if you can run Vampire, you can run Demon, but there is also other stuff to do in Demon.<br /> <br /> Mummy and LoE are 90% remembering things. If you can remember it, it's mostly errand gaming.<br /> <br /> Orpheus is one long adventure, and if you don't like it, the base game has lot's of good fodder. Corporate espionage and horror! Two great tastes that taste great together!<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T06:52:23-08:00","id":330092,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure which of the games I'd say is the hardest to run, but I can list some pitfalls at the top of my head:<br /> <br /> Vampire - Wheels within wheels. As presented, in the game elder vampires are fighting a shadow war against each other, played out through games of subterfuge and plots reaching down through the ranks. The elders themselves are playthings of ancient methuselah vampires whose moves in the Jyhad play out over centuries. If your game is going to take the War of Ages into account, then you need to start watching/reading a bunch of heist/spy/conspiracy/double-cross fiction. You should probably also read up a bit on the real world history of the setting you've chosen for your game, and decide which, if any, real world events were orchestrated by the elders and the methuselahs in your setting.<br /> <br /> Demon - Demons fuel their powers through Faith. Faith offered up by a human being to the demon. Think about that. How do you as a storyteller portray this reaping of faith in a way that comes off as believable and truthful? Then again, maybe it is my atheist upbringing that acts as a speedbump in this case.<br /> <br /> Mummy - You have to familiarize yourself with the setting of another game, most likely. Mummy has always been a crossover game, which means that you as a storyteller will have a bit of heavy lifting ahead of you. Not only do you need to mix and match game mechanics, you also have to mix and match <i>themes</i>. Introducing elements of Mummy - a game of occultism, moral reflection and mystery - into a game of Werewolf - a game filled with glorious combat, dark satire and splatter punk - is a challenge. Yes, they are both fighting the Wyrm, but they do so in very different ways. And that's before we get into the mechanics, let alone the Umbra. Now take these problems, and apply them to every other game that you wish to cross Mummy over with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php\" target=\"_blank\">Malkavian Madness Forum</a> - Your pbp fix. Be it nWoD, cWoD, CoC, D&amp;D or something else entirely, come over here and get your game on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/348-infernalgoose","name":"InfernalGoose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T20:21:31-08:00","id":330733,"title":"","content":"Changeling was tricky from a rules point of view, but easy for me thematically. That being said, I love Changeling with a deep passion, so you know there's that. But honestly,if you tweak the rules a bit, I find that Changeling can be done in a wide variety of themes which makes it easier, imho. I never got to run Mummy, but that struck me as clunky as well. Demon is great conceptually, but my players never really connected with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2197-roleplayrose","name":"roleplayrose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2197_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T14:39:57-08:00","id":331500,"title":"","content":"Changeling because it always comes down to &quot;what happens when you climb a chimerical ladder&quot; always that's where the game always breaks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T01:11:25-08:00","id":339823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/314143-the-hardest-games-to-run-and-why#post314143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...theres a lot of info to cover..</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand. I want it all in the game. I want my Mages, Wraiths, Vampires, Werewolves, Changelings, Mummies, and yes even the Gypsies. That is the hardest campaign to run.<br /> <br /> Still, for single game, I would put them in order Changling, Wraith, then Werewolf.<br /> <br /> Changeling to me was beautiful in concept but the powers simply were incomprehensibly chaotic to me. It always seemed like the possibility of doing something was largely accidental - that there was no way of knowing whether or not anything you had would actually be usable in play. Vampire, Mage, Wraith, Werewolf, etc. you knew you could always count on spending your supernatural advantage (essence, gnosis, blood, etc.) to do something. Changeling was a random draw of the cards or so it seemed.<br /> <br /> Wraith as a game of attempting to overcome the traumas in one's life and transcend to the light is gorgeous. The idea of handing over my alter-egos shadow self to a friend to play against me seemed socially dangerous - especially if they know me too well. I always felt the original wraith should be refereed only by a licensed practicing psychologist with heavy group management skills as well as a minimum of a minor in theatrical production.<br /> <br /> Werewolf has complicated mechanics to me. It isn't the effects in the game but the keeping track of all the forms, functions, and forms of reputation for each and every NPC and PC. The seemingly massive list of conditional reasons why something would be <i>'X, Y, or Z if but not when and then over there'</i> left me loving the werewolf lore and unwilling to play a werewolf. After all, at the time I was also studying for straight A's on college exams in multiple subjects in which my talent was limited and my interest negligible so that I could study what I was really after...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cIt was clear to me for a long time that the origins of science had their deep roots in a particular myth, that of invariance.&quot; ~ Giorgio de Santillana<br /> Preface to Hamlet's Mill","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2345-whithers","name":"Whithers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2345_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T01:23:28-08:00","id":339834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>InfernalGoose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/314143-the-hardest-games-to-run-and-why?p=330092#post330092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Demon - Demons fuel their powers through Faith. Faith offered up by a human being to the demon. Think about that. How do you as a storyteller portray this reaping of faith in a way that comes off as believable and truthful? Then again, maybe it is my atheist upbringing that acts as a speedbump in this case.</div> </div> </div> </div>To quote from a couple examples of scripture - Heb. 11:1: &quot;Now faith is the assurance of things hoped for, the evidence of things not seen.&quot; or &quot;Now faith is the conviction concerning those things that are in hope, as if it were these things in action, and the revelation of those things that are unseen;&quot;<br /> <br /> A person who encounters a Demon, even ephemerally, holds a sure knowledge of those things that are unseen, and therefore hopes in the results of those actions and rewards of which that experience implies and infers are possible. The reaping of power from such trust by a demon is believable to me; it is certainly believable if one considers the election of politicians - is it not?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cIt was clear to me for a long time that the origins of science had their deep roots in a particular myth, that of invariance.&quot; ~ Giorgio de Santillana<br /> Preface to Hamlet's Mill","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2345-whithers","name":"Whithers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2345_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}